Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 23:52:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 058/106] ASoC: qcom: q6voice: log the vocproc ports at call
 setup

One dev_info line showing the Tx/Rx mixer indices and resolved AFE port
ids when the vocproc is created - invaluable while chasing routing
problems (confirmed tx_port=120 -> AFE 45111 = TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_3 during
the uplink debugging that led to the topology fix).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice.c
index 211b1df4f..f035fb861 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6voice.c
@@ -177,6 +177,9 @@ static int q6voice_path_start(struct q6voice_path *p)
 
 	cvp = p->runtime->sessions[Q6VOICE_SERVICE_CVP];
 	if (!cvp) {
+		dev_info(dev, "creating cvp: tx_port=%d (afe %d) rx_port=%d (afe %d)\n",
+			 p->tx_port, q6afe_get_port_id(p->tx_port),
+			 p->rx_port, q6afe_get_port_id(p->rx_port));
 		cvp = q6cvp_session_create(p->type,
 					   q6afe_get_port_id(p->tx_port),
 					   q6afe_get_port_id(p->rx_port));
-- 
